PURPOSE of /kernel/misc/self-poweroff
Description: Powers itself off
Author: Erico Nunes <ernunes@redhat.com>

Powers itself off.

This is intended to be used by the Guest in a Beaker job using a
<guestrecipe>.
When using it, the Guest powers off to allow the Host machine to safely
modify the guest settings (such as VM configuration, firmware settings).
The Host should then power it back on in a separate further task.

See also: /kernel/misc/wait-guest-poweroff
